n.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-08-11T03:37:24Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#31455848227", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Pedro Téllez-Girón, 1st Duke of Osuna, 5th count of Ureña was a Spanish nobleman and administrator.", "newValue": "Pedro Téllez-Girón, 1st Duke of Osuna and 5th Count of Ureña (born 1537-08-08 in Osuna), was a preeminent Spanish grandee and administrator whose career under King Philip II solidified Habsburg power in the Mediterranean and within the Iberian Peninsula. As one of the most influential noblemen of his era, Téllez-Girón managed vast estates, commanded military forces, and served in key imperial positions, notably as Viceroy of Naples from 1582 to 1586. His tenure reflected the complex interplay of aristocratic privilege, centralized royal authority, and geopolitical challenges that defined the Spanish Golden Age.

